# N5 (SOFT): the lanes L2 plan, round-timing, audits off: P(4), P(3), P(2) and the lone user's rate on today's engines in one boot per
# context (4k, 32k), and D0 (the one-user 16-row block) against those engines for a lone coding user (tokens per round and tok/s).
# PROFILE NOTE: the lanes profiles are NOT the best config. The attach refuses the fused commit when the solo lane (D0) is on, and the
# lanes profiles are the gate profile plus their lane flags and the K/V slide; lanes with the fused commit or the vglue levers is in
# no profile. The gate plan picks its own lanes profile (lanes-exact c2-packed-tp4-lanes-gate; round-timing and lanes-timing
# c2-packed-tp4-lanes-time-gate), as in tp4-lanes-jobs; C2_PROFILE names the gate base it is run from. So this job judges the lanes
# programme on the gate-era engines, not on the best config; compare it with N4 only for the round shapes.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/next window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed
# from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image N0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1 is a PLACEHOLDER: the driver of the window may substitute it (in every template) once the image is built
# from the pushed branch; the driver's IMAGE_TAG env overrides it.
# Duration (estimate): 45-100 min (five arms).
# SOFT: a failed arm is logged and the window goes on; the product is the round times.
# Read: the gate summary per arm; P per live count; D0 against the per-request engine for the lone user; the [LANE] engaged lines.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate
C2_GATE_PLAN=round-timing
C2_GATE_JIT=record
